          "text": "{\"persuasion\":\"PERSUADED\",\"support_scope\":\"FULL\",\"rationale\":\"The entry’s core identification is directly stated in Psalm 119:142: “thy law is the truth.” Its description of the law as “the standard” is a natural account of what law does—provides the authoritative measure for conduct and judgment—and is reinforced by the chapter’s comparison of truth with God’s word and commandments. The strongest counter-reading rightly observes that biblical truth is broader in many contexts, especially where Christ, God’s word, or the gospel is called truth. But that reading includes rather than displaces the identification of God’s law with truth. Under the stated scope rules, a broader complementary interpretation is not a defeating rival.\",\"book_core_identification\":\"“The truth” identifies God’s law.\",\"book_secondary_elaborations\":[\"God’s law functions as the standard or authoritative measure.\"],\"unsupported_glossary_assertions\":[],\"chapter_only_objections\":[\"The chapter’s claim that the definite article in John 14:6 establishes a uniquely scripturally encoded meaning is not demonstrated merely by the word “the.”\",\"The equation of every relevant occurrence of “the truth” with the covenant law may be too uniform; some contexts directly emphasize Christ, the gospel, divine faithfulness, or truthful conduct.\",\"Calling Christ “the Torah embodied” is a broader Christological synthesis requiring more argument than the glossary entry itself asserts.\",\"The chapter’s interpretation of the Edenic sword as preserving rather than barring access to the tree of life is contestable and unnecessary to support the glossary entry.\"],\"strongest_counter_interpretation\":\"“The truth” is God’s revealed reality and saving word, supremely embodied in Jesus Christ; God’s law is one true and authoritative expression of that revelation but is not the term’s exhaustive biblical referent.\",\"counter_core_identification\":\"God’s revealed reality and word, personally embodied in Christ, with the law as one included expression.\",\"counter_relation_to_book_core\":\"SAME_CORE_BROADER\",\"material_core_denial\":\"None. The strongest counter-reading denies only that “God’s law” exhausts every biblical use of “the truth”; it does not deny Psalm 119:142’s explicit identification or the law’s role as an authoritative standard.\",\"counter_case\":[\"John 14:6 directly predicates “the truth” of Jesus himself.\",\"John 17:17 identifies God’s word as truth, a category potentially broader than law alone.\",\"In 2 John 4, walking in truth occurs “as” commanded by the Father, which can distinguish truth from the commandment while closely relating them.\",\"Other biblical contexts use truth for the gospel, apostolic teaching, divine faithfulness, and ethical integrity.\"],\"book_explanatory_advantages\":[\"Psalm 119:142 supplies an explicit copular identification: “thy law is the truth,” not merely “thy law is true.”\",\"The description “the standard” succinctly explains the normative function of law.\",\"The relationship between truth and commanded conduct in 2 John coheres naturally with a law-centered identification.\",\"The chapter offers a coherent way to relate Christological truth language to the law by treating Christ as the standard embodied and lived.\"],\"counter_explanatory_advantages\":[\"It accounts more naturally for the direct personal predicate in John 14:6 without first identifying Christ with Torah.\",\"It accommodates the breadth of biblical truth language across Christ, word, gospel, faithfulness, doctrine, and conduct.\",\"It avoids requiring one uniform symbolic referent in every context.\"],\"evidence_book_core_cannot_explain\":[],\"comparative_winner\":\"BOOK\",\"decisive_sources\":[\"Psalm 119:142\",\"2 John 4\",\"John 17:17\",\"John 14:6\"],\"unresolved_objections\":[\"The entry is narrower than the full biblical semantic range of “truth.”\",\"Psalm 119:142 decisively establishes the law as truth, but by itself does not prove that every occurrence of “the truth” exclusively denotes law.\",\"The Christ-as-embodied-law synthesis is plausible but less textually immediate than the ordinary Christological reading of John 14:6.\"],\"confidence\":\"medium\"}"
        }
